  "notes": "Native-rate campaign, 18-20 Sep 2026, RunPod RTX PRO 6000, CARLA 0.9.15 Epic. Driven at 2 Hz, set with PADDOCK_INFER_HZ; drivejepa/model.yaml declares no planning rate, so 2 Hz is the operator's choice and not a registry value. routes_file, routes_subset and waypoint_dt are identical to the 20 Hz pooled50 run; that run recorded MKL/OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 and this one 4, which changes throughput and not the trajectory. The simulator build and the shared tracker and controller were the same, and are recorded in neither run. NAVSIM-v2 checkpoint zero-shot, front pair. 50 of 50 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to drivejepa on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 50/50 source runs recorded. PADDOCK_INFER_HZ was supplied by the ingest config and recorded by no source run, so it is the operator's assertion about the campaign, not a reading from it. driven at 2 Hz, not the 20 Hz the benchmark's published protocol calls the model at, so this run is kept and does not rank against runs that were -- the paired comparison is docs/benchmarks/bench2drive-native-rate.md.",
